(footprint "TRANS_SOT-416_EMT3-EMT3F_ROHM"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "ROHM EMT3 / EMT3F (SOT-416 / SOT-416FL, 1.6 x 0.8 mm) 3-lead digital-transistor land. Copper is ROHM's own recommended pattern (Land Pattern Reference, Transistor, Rev.001 p.1/6, heading \"EMT3/EMT3F (1.6x0.8)\"): the two same-side pads 0.6 x 0.7 mm on 1.0 mm pitch, the lone pad 0.7 x 0.7 mm (deliberately wider - that lead is the widest terminal in the family), rows 1.3 mm centre-to-centre. ROHM publishes ONE land for both the gull-wing EMT3 and the flat-lead EMT3F, so this single footprint correctly serves both; do not draw a second. Widened 2026-08-26 from an inherited imperial-grid pattern (0.3556 x 0.762 mm, 14 x 30 mil) that was ~30-50 percent narrow across the lead and left almost no side fillet on the lone pad. Courtyard is copper extent + 0.25 mm.")
	(tags "ROHM EMT3 EMT3F SOT-416 SOT-416FL digital transistor 3-lead smd")
